{/* Generated by apps/docs/scripts/generate.py from apps/docs/data/index.mdx.in and tracked data files; edit the template, not this file. */}

XDRCheck is a test kit for software that reads the Stellar ledger. Stellar encodes every transaction and ledger in
XDR (External Data Representation, a binary format). The kit holds a corpus of ledgers and values whose shape is
rare but valid: a muxed account, a signed-payload signer, a fee bump around a failed transaction, a deeply nested
authorization tree. Each corpus entry is tagged with the CAP (Core Advancement Proposal) that introduced its shape
and states the values a correct reader must produce. It is for maintainers of Stellar SDKs and XDR libraries, and
for authors and operators of indexers: programs that read ledgers into a store.

