## What it checks

The same corpus tests three kinds of code.

| You have | The kit checks | With |
|---|---|---|
| An SDK or XDR library | that the decoder reads every entry, consumes every byte, re-encodes the identical bytes and produces the expected values | `xdrcheck conform`, or a test recipe in your own repository ([Conformance](/architecture/conformance)) |
| An indexer | that the rows it stored for each ledger agree with the entry: transactions, participants, state changes, movements and addresses | `xdrcheck replay` and a small adapter ([Replay](/architecture/replay)) |
| Go ingestion code on go-stellar-sdk | the code patterns behind those errors, such as trusting a field stellar-core does not validate, walking a recursive structure without a bound, or taking participants from the envelope instead of the meta | `xdrlint` ([Linter and guide](/architecture/linter-and-guide)) |

What the runs have checked so far. Each figure is generated from a tracked file and links to the page that says how
it was made and how to run it again.

- **Corpus.** @@entries@@ entries. @@both_passphrases@@ were produced by a local, offline stellar-core under both
  the testnet and the mainnet passphrase, @@captured@@ were captured from network history and @@golden@@ come from
  stellar-core's own goldens. The @@synthetic@@ hand-made entries are marked `synthetic`.
  [Read an entry](/start/read-an-entry)
- **Pubnet ledgers @@scan_first@@ to @@scan_last@@.** @@scan_ledgers@@ ledgers and @@scan_txs@@ transactions were
  read from the public data lake, decoded, re-encoded byte for byte and hash-checked: @@scan_refusals@@ ledgers
  refused and @@scan_mismatches@@ mismatches over @@scan_links@@ header hash-chain links. The scan computes shapes
  and these checks; no pipeline or SDK was replayed over all of it. [Mainnet scan](/results/mainnet-scan)
- **Public incidents.** Three wallet-backend incidents and three js-stellar-sdk incidents fail on their pre-fix
  versions and pass on the fixed ones (`make verify-replay`, `make verify-conformance`).
  @@known_defects_reproduced@@ of the @@known_defects_total@@ public incidents on that page are reproduced this
  way; the others are run, checked or held as corpus input. [Known incidents](/results/incidents)
- **SDKs side by side.** @@sdk_columns@@ columns (releases of the @@sdk_names@@ SDKs, and stellar-core) in one
  conformance matrix, so a defect found in one SDK is checked in the others. [SDK matrix](/results/sdk-matrix)
- **Findings.** @@findings_total@@ findings with a public record, @@findings_filed@@ of them filed upstream.
  [Findings](/results/findings)

## Who these docs are for

| You are | Start with | Then |
|---|---|---|
| A maintainer of a Stellar SDK or XDR library | [Start here: SDK maintainers](/start/for-sdk-maintainers) | [Add to CI](/guides/sdk-ci), [Protocol upgrades](/guides/protocol-upgrade-sdk) |
| An author or operator of an indexer | [Start here: indexer authors](/start/for-indexers) | [Go adapter](/guides/go-indexer), [Lint your code](/guides/lint-go), [CI recipes](/guides/ci), [Hardening guide](/hardening/overview) |
| A Stellar developer new to ledger data | [XDR and ledger data](/concepts/xdr-and-ledger-data) | [Shapes and CAPs](/concepts/shapes-and-caps), [Read an entry](/start/read-an-entry) |
| Someone who needs a shape the corpus lacks | [Add corpus entries](/guides/add-corpus-entries) | [Manifest](/reference/manifest), [Entry IDs](/reference/entry-ids) |

The site has four tabs. **Guides** holds the tasks, by role. **Technical overview** says how each part works.
**Results** holds what the runs found. **Reference** holds every command, file format and protocol.

## What it runs against

Every version the kit builds against or tests is pinned in `pins.toml`. `xdrcheck pins check` rejects a version
named anywhere else.

| Component | Pinned in `pins.toml` | Role |
|---|---|---|
| Stellar protocol | @@pin_protocol@@ | the highest protocol the kit supports |
| stellar-core | @@pin_core@@ | emits corpus ledgers on a local, offline node; a decoder column |
| XDR definitions (stellar-xdr) | tag `@@pin_xdr@@` | the type system of the corpus and the scan |
| rs-stellar-xdr | @@pin_rs_xdr@@; columns @@cols_rust@@ | the oracle that decodes and re-encodes every entry; SDK under test |
| js-stellar-sdk | columns @@cols_js@@ | SDK under test |
| go-stellar-sdk | columns @@cols_go@@ | SDK under test; the library `xdrlint` analyses |
| py-stellar-base | columns @@cols_python@@ | SDK under test |
| wallet-backend | commit `@@pin_wallet_backend@@` | indexer under replay |
| stellar-etl | @@pin_stellar_etl@@ | indexer under replay |
| Horizon | not pinned; the version is given on each run | indexer under its service rig |

A column is one SDK at one pinned version. `drivers/sets.toml` groups the columns into named sets, and
`xdrcheck conform run --set NAME` runs one of them; the `required` set is @@set_required@@. Every component, what
the kit takes from it and what it gives back are on [Stellar integration](/architecture/stellar-integration).
